From 9619d06f3a03190a296ebcc50662e4d214723891 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: James Trotter <james@jamesat.dev>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 07:55:24 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] channels: auto-register new channels, expire inactive
 registrations

Two new options under channels.registration:

auto-register: a channel created by a logged-in client (by joining it) is
registered to their account at once, as if they had sent /CS REGISTER, with
the same restrictions (enabled, operator-only, max-channels-per-account)
and the usual ChanServ notice and +q.

expire-after: a registered channel with no JOIN, PRIVMSG or NOTICE for that
long is unregistered (logged, LocalChannels snomask, NOTICE to the founder
if online). The founder is warned up to a week before: once on the periodic
check if online, and at every login during the warning period. Operators
with chanreg can exempt a channel with /CS SET #channel EXPIRY OFF;
/CS GET #channel EXPIRY shows when it will expire.

Activity is tracked in memory on every message and stored with the
channel registration (LastActivity) at most once an hour per channel.
Registrations from before this change start their clock at the first
check. Both options default to off.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
