diff --git a/docs/MANUAL.md b/docs/MANUAL.md
index 15cda167..3d260737 100644
--- a/docs/MANUAL.md
+++ b/docs/MANUAL.md
@@ -366,6 +366,10 @@ For example, `/CS REGISTER #channel` will register the channel `#channel` to my
 
 If your friends have registered accounts, you can automatically grant them operator permissions when they join the channel. For more details, see `/CS HELP AMODE`.
 
+Server administrators can make this automatic: with `channels.registration.auto-register` enabled, a new channel is registered to your account as soon as you create it by joining it (while logged in), subject to the same restrictions as `/CS REGISTER` (`operator-only`, `max-channels-per-account`).
+
+With `channels.registration.expire-after` set (e.g., `90d`), registered channels that have had no activity (nobody joining or sending a `PRIVMSG` or `NOTICE` to them) for that long are unregistered automatically, which frees the name for someone else. The founder gets a notice from ChanServ a week before (if they're online, and again whenever they log in during that week); using the channel restarts the clock. `/CS GET #channel EXPIRY` shows when a channel will expire, and operators with the `chanreg` capability can exempt a channel with `/CS SET #channel EXPIRY OFF`.
+
 
